Build a production-grade, local-first, highly specialized security testing engine suite focused exclusively on the four highest-impact vulnerability classes that directly enable either (A) unauthorized wallet/balance credit or (B) unpaid item fulfillment. The target is modern web applications as of October 2026: SPAs, GraphQL/REST hybrids, serverless backends, edge functions, and payment flows involving third-party gateways. The engines must be extremely deep, high-signal, and effective against real-world targets. No superficial scanning. Every detection technique must be state-of-the-art and produce concrete, reproducible evidence tied to observable side-effects (balance change, order status change, new entitlement, download link appearance, etc.).

### Strict scope – only these four engines
1. Access control / API authorization (BOLA, IDOR, BFLA, tenant isolation, object-level and function-level authorization failures)
2. Payment integration integrity (webhook verification failures, amount/currency mismatch, client-trusted confirmation, replay, confirm-before-capture, signature bypass)
3. Concurrency, idempotency & replay (race conditions on credit/debit/fulfill/redeem, weak or missing idempotency, double-spend, exactly-once violations)
4. Input validation & parameter integrity (client-controlled monetary and quantity parameters, missing server-side price re-derivation, type confusion, business-logic parameter abuse)

All other vulnerability classes are out of scope for this module set.

